## Adding a New Model

Use `ds-cli` to scaffold a new model directory:

```bash
ds-cli add-model . --model-name <model_name> --model-type Classification
# or
ds-cli add-model . --model-name <model_name> --model-type Regression
```

After generation:
1. Open `src/{{ project }}/models/<model_name>/config/hyper_config.py`
2. Fill in `id_col`, `target`, `num_cols`, `redu_col`
3. Adjust hyperparameter search spaces as needed

---

## Adding a New Dataset

```bash
ds-cli add-dataset . --dataset-name <dataset_name>
```

After generation:
1. Open `src/{{ project }}/dataflow/config/<dataset_name>_config.py` — add domain-specific config keys
2. Open `src/{{ project }}/dataflow/preprocess/<dataset_name>_preprocess.py` — implement `coerce_types()` and `transform()`
3. Open `src/{{ project }}/dataflow/features/<dataset_name>_features.py` — implement `_engineer()` with your feature logic

---

## Removing a Model or Dataset

```bash
ds-cli remove-model . --model-name <model_name>
ds-cli remove-dataset . --dataset-name <dataset_name>
```

